s the docstring requirements. "\n                        "Ensure that the function signature matches exactly and all edge cases are handled.",\n            context=self.problem_text\n        )\n\n        candidate2 = await self.generate(\n            instruction=f"Based on the analysis: {analysis}\\n"\n                        "Generate an alternative Python function implementation that satisfies the docstring requirements. "\n                        "Ensure that the function signature matches exactly and all edge cases are handled.",\n            context=self.problem_text\n        )\n\n        # Step 4: Revise the candidates to improve quality\n        revised_candidate1 = await self.revise(\n            instruction="Critique and refine the first candidate solution. Ensure that it is correct, efficient, and adheres to the docstring specifications.",\n            context=candidate1\n        )\n\n        revised_candidate2 = await self.revise(\n            instruction="Critique and refine the second candidate solution. Ensure that it is correct, efficient, and adheres to the docstring specifications.",\n            context=candidate2\n        )\n\n        # Step 5: Ensemble the candidates to select the best solution\n        final_solution = await self.ensemble(\n            instruction="Evaluate the two revised candidate solutions. Select the one that best satisfies the docstring requirements, "\n                        "handles all edge cases, and is efficient. Provide the final Python function implementation.",\n            contexts=[revised_candidate1, revised_candidate2]\n        )\n\n        return final_solution\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.problem_text = problem\n        self.llm = create(config)\n        \n        self.generate = operator.Generate(self.l