on that satisfies the following:\n        - Matches the function signature exactly\n        - Follows the docstring description\n        - Handles all examples and edge cases mentioned\n        - Returns the expected output format\n        - Includes necessary imports if required\n        """\n        initial_implementation = await self.generate(instruction=initial_implementation_instruction, context=self.problem_text)\n\n        # Step 3: Revise the initial implementation for correctness and efficiency\n        revision_instruction = """\n        Critique the provided implementation and refine it to ensure:\n        - Correctness: The function passes all test cases implied by the docstring\n        - Efficiency: The solution is optimized for performance\n        - Readability: The code is well-structured and easy to understand\n        - Edge Cases: All edge cases mentioned in the docstring are handled\n        """\n        revised_implementation = await self.revise(instruction=revision_instruction, context=initial_implementation)\n\n        # Step 4: Summarize the final implementation\n        summary_instruction = """\n        Provide a concise summary of the final implementation, highlighting:\n        - The approach taken to solve the problem\n        - Key decisions made during the implementation\n        - How the solution handles edge cases and special conditions\n        - The efficiency and correctness of the solution\n        """\n        final_summary = await self.summarize(instruction=summary_instruction, context=revised_implementation)\n\n        # Step 5: Ensemble to select the best solution\n        ensemble_instruction = """\n        Evaluate the following candidate solutions and select the best one:\n        - Candidate 1: Initial Implementation\n        - Candidate 2: Revised Implementation\n        Choose the solution that:\n        - Is most correct and passes all test cases\n        - Is most efficient\n        - Is most readable and well-struc